{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y8zfXoaY96dTKeMzH8owZC","type":"tool_result","content":"internal/cli/cmd_config.go:11:\t\tUse:   \"config\",\ninternal/cli/cmd_config.go:17:\t\tUse:   \"check\",\ninternal/cli/cmd_labels.go:11:\t\tUse:   \"labels\",\ninternal/cli/cmd_labels.go:16:\t\tUse:   \"sync\",\ninternal/cli/cmd_setup.go:13:\t\tUse:   \"setup\",\ninternal/cli/cmd_setup.go:32:\tf.BoolVar(&o.Check, \"check\", false, \"report only; exit 2 when anything has drifted\")\ninternal/setupcmd/appmanifest.go:55:\t\tName:               name,\ninternal/setupcmd/cmd.go:39:\t\tif err := CreateApp(ctx, e, repo, CreateAppOpts{Name: o.AppName, KeyPath: o.KeyFile, Force: o.Force}); err != nil {\ninternal/setupcmd/cmd.go:75:// manual steps are needed.\ninternal/setupcmd/cmd.go:86:\t\treturn errors.New(\"setup: manual steps needed\")\ninternal/setupcmd/policy.go:79:\t\treturn Row{Name: rulesetName, Status: StatusOK, Detail: policyBranch + \" requires a pull request; only the ard App bypasses\"}\ninternal/setupcmd/policy.go:81:\treturn Row{Name: rulesetName, Status: StatusDrift, Detail: strings.Join(problems, \"; \") + \". Fix in \" + rulesURL(repo)}\ninternal/setupcmd/policy.go:93:\t\treturn Row{Name: appPermName, Status: StatusOK, Detail: \"no workflows or administration permission\"}\ninternal/setupcmd/policy.go:95:\treturn Row{Name: appPermName, Status: StatusDrift, Detail: \"the App has the \" + strings.Join(bad, \", \") + \" permission; remove it in \" + installURL(repo)}\ninternal/setupcmd/policy.go:101:\t\treturn Row{Name: mergeName, Status: StatusDrift, Detail: fmt.Sprintf(\"allow_rebase_merge is on while %s is on; run: gh api -X PATCH repos/%s -F allow_rebase_merge=false\", policyVersioning, repo)}\ninternal/setupcmd/policy.go:103:\treturn Row{Name: mergeName, Status: StatusOK, Detail: \"merge settings match the policy\"}\ninternal/setupcmd/report.go:18:\tStatusManual  Status = \"manual\"\ninternal/setupcmd/report.go:21:// Row is one line of the report. For a manual row Detail is the exact fix.\ninternal/setupcmd/report.go:31:// Green reports whether no row is drift or manual.\ninternal/setupcmd/report.go:51:// Print writes one line per row. A manual row reads \"manual: <fix>\".\ninternal/setupcmd/report.go:58:\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(w, \"manual: %s: %s\\n\", x.Name, x.Detail)\ninternal/setupcmd/setup.go:66:\tperm := Row{Name: permName, Status: StatusOK}\ninternal/setupcmd/setup.go:90:\trow := Row{Name: labelName, Status: StatusOK}\ninternal/setupcmd/setup.go:111:\trow = Row{Name: labelName, Status: StatusChanged}\ninternal/setupcmd/setup.go:119:\t\trow = Row{Name: labelName, Status: StatusManual, Detail: \"create or update these labels by hand: \" + strings.Join(names, \", \")}\ninternal/setupcmd/setup.go:130:// read gives a manual row with the exact command to look it up by hand.\ninternal/setupcmd/setup.go:133:\tmanual := func(name, detail string) Row { return Row{Name: name, Status: StatusManual, Detail: detail} }\ninternal/setupcmd/setup.go:153:\t\trows = append(rows, manual(rulesetName, \"admin read is needed; check \"+rulesURL(repo)+\" or run: gh api repos/\"+repo.String()+\"/rulesets\"))\ninternal/setupcmd/setup.go:155:\t\trows = append(rows, manual(rulesetName, \"cannot resolve the App; run: \"+appCmd))\ninternal/setupcmd/setup.go:160:\t\trows = append(rows, manual(appPermName, \"cannot read the App; run: \"+appCmd+\" and check the permissions at \"+installURL(repo)))\ninternal/setupcmd/setup.go:170:\t\treturn append(rows, manual(mergeName, \"cannot read merge settings; run: gh api repos/\"+repo.String())), nil\ninternal/setupcmd/setup.go:177:\t\treturn append(rows, manual(mergeName, fmt.Sprintf(\"cannot read the %s variable; run: gh variable get %s -R %s\", policyVersioning, policyVersioning, repo))), nil\nGitHub labels prefixed `ard:` are the queue and the state machine. `.ard/<issue#>/` in the target repository holds each issue's plan, per-role summaries and full agent logs.\n\n## Configuration by convention\n\nA target repository opts in with an `.ard/` directory. A role exists because its directory exists:\n\n```\n.ard/\n├── config.yaml          # global settings and overrides only\n├── scanners/<name>/     # scan (executable) or prompt.txt; optional Dockerfile, scripts\n├── triage/<name>/       # prompt.txt; optional Dockerfile, scripts\n├── workers/<name>/      # prompt.txt; optional Dockerfile, scripts\n├── reviewers/<name>/    # prompt.txt; optional Dockerfile, scripts\n└── <issue#>/            # per-issue output and logs, written only by ard\n```\n\nSee [Configuration](docs/proposal.md#configuration) in the proposal for the full schema and defaults.\n\n## Development","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d3d22016-c02a-4824-9a50-9b114b5bbbcd","uuid":"da45737c-4742-41c7-9d72-0b90d45a37f9","timestamp":"2026-11-25T12:01:18.046Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"internal/cli/cmd_config.go:11:\t\tUse:   \"config\",\ninternal/cli/cmd_config.go:17:\t\tUse:   \"check\",\ninternal/cli/cmd_labels.go:11:\t\tUse:   \"labels\",\ninternal/cli/cmd_labels.go:16:\t\tUse:   \"sync\",\ninternal/cli/cmd_setup.go:13:\t\tUse:   \"setup\",\ninternal/cli/cmd_setup.go:32:\tf.BoolVar(&o.Check, \"check\", false, \"report only; exit 2 when anything has drifted\")\ninternal/setupcmd/appmanifest.go:55:\t\tName:               name,\ninternal/setupcmd/cmd.go:39:\t\tif err := CreateApp(ctx, e, repo, CreateAppOpts{Name: o.AppName, KeyPath: o.KeyFile, Force: o.Force}); err != nil {\ninternal/setupcmd/cmd.go:75:// manual steps are needed.\ninternal/setupcmd/cmd.go:86:\t\treturn errors.New(\"setup: manual steps needed\")\ninternal/setupcmd/policy.go:79:\t\treturn Row{Name: rulesetName, Status: StatusOK, Detail: policyBranch + \" requires a pull request; only the ard App bypasses\"}\ninternal/setupcmd/policy.go:81:\treturn Row{Name: rulesetName, Status: StatusDrift, Detail: strings.Join(problems, \"; \") + \". Fix in \" + rulesURL(repo)}\ninternal/setupcmd/pol